horde/vergen/issues/508","id":4717314799,"node_id":"I_kwDOAdPyIs8AAAABGSyC7w","number":508,"title":"vergen-gitcl 10.0.0 doesn't fall back to idempotet variables","user":{"login":"Tiwalun","id":859555,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1OTU1NQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/859555?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tiwalun","html_url":"https://github.com/Tiwalun","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tiwalun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tiwalun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tiwalun/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tiwalun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tiwalun/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tiwalun/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tiwalun/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tiwalun/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tiwalun/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-06-22T13:58:22Z","updated_at":"2026-06-24T16:16:01Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"After updating to `vergen-gitcl` v10.0.0, I get the following error when trying to build a project outside a git worktree:\n\n```\nwarning: <crate>@0.27.0: not within a suitable 'git' worktree!\nwarning: <crate>@0.27.0: Unable to set VERGEN_GIT_BRANCH\nwarning: <crate>@0.27.0: Unable to set VERGEN_GIT_COMMIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL\nwarning: <crate>@0.27.0: Unable to set VERGEN_GIT_COMMIT_AUTHOR_NAME\nwarning: <crate>@0.27.0: Unable to set VERGEN_GIT_COMMIT_COUNT\nwarning: <crate>@0.27.0: Unable to set VERGEN_GIT_COMMIT_DATE\nwarning: <crate>@0.27.0: Unable to set VERGEN_GIT_COMMIT_MESSAGE\nwarning: <crate>@0.27.0: Unable to set VERGEN_GIT_COMMIT_TIMESTAMP\nwarning: <crate>@0.27.0: Unable to set VERGEN_GIT_DESCRIBE\nwarning: <crate>@0.27.0: Unable to set VERGEN_GIT_SHA\nwarning: <crate>@0.27.0: Unable to set VERGEN_GIT_DIRTY\n```\nWith the previous version, this would set the variables to a default:\n\n```\nwarning: <crate>@0.27.0: not within a suitable 'git' worktree!\nwarning: <crate>@0.27.0: VERGEN_GIT_BRANCH set to default\nwarning: <crate>@0.27.0: VERGEN_GIT_COMMIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL set to default\nwarning: <crate>@0.27.0: VERGEN_GIT_COMMIT_AUTHOR_NAME set to default\nwarning: <crate>@0.27.0: VERGEN_GIT_COMMIT_COUNT set to default\nwarning: <crate>@0.27.0: VERGEN_GIT_COMMIT_DATE set to default\nwarning: <crate>@0.27.0: VERGEN_GIT_COMMIT_MESSAGE set to default\nwarning: <crate>@0.27.0: VERGEN_GIT_COMMIT_TIMESTAMP set to default\nwarning: <crate>@0.27.0: VERGEN_GIT_DESCRIBE set to default\nwarning: <crate>@0.27.0: VERGEN_GIT_SHA set to default\nwarning: <crate>@0.27.0: VERGEN_GIT_DIRTY set to default\n```\n\nIs this a bug? Or if this is intentional, is there a way to get back the previous behavior, by setting a flag?","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rustyhorde/vergen/issues/508/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rustyhorde/vergen/issues/508/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"reopened","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rustyhorde/vergen/issues/299","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rustyhorde/vergen","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rustyhorde/vergen/issues/299/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rustyhorde/vergen/issues/299/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rustyhorde/vergen/issues/299/events","html_url":"https://github.com/rustyhorde/vergen/issues/299","id":2091257500,"node_id":"I_kwDOAdPyIs58pg6c","number":299,"title":"Environment values should not be `VERGEN_IDEMPOTENT_OUTPUT` on failure","user":{"login":"holly-hacker","id":13605369,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjA1MzY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13605369?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/holly-hacker","html_url":"https://github.com/holly-hacker","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/holly-hacker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/holly-hacker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/holly-hacker/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/holly-hacker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/holly-hacker/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/holly-hacker/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/holly-hacker/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/holly-hacker/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/holly-hacker/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":7,"created_at":"2024-01-19T19:45:20Z","updated_at":"2025-04-12T22:34:45Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I am using the following configuration:\r\n```rs\r\npub fn main() {\r\n    vergen::EmitBuilder::builder()\r\n        .idempotent()\r\n        .quiet()\r\n        .all_cargo()\r\n        .all_git()\r\n        .git_describe(true, false, None)\r\n        .all_rustc()\r\n        .emit()\r\n        .unwrap();\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nDue to an error on my end, there was no `.git` folder in my build environment which means the git env vars could not be populated correctly. However, the value of each git environment value was `VERGEN_IDEMPOTENT_OUTPUT` which is very unexpected and cost me a lot of time troubleshooting in the wrong direction. Ideally, these should be filled with another value to indicate the error.\r\n\r\nI understand that the `.quiet()` call and lack of `.fail_on_error()` make this error harder to spot, but I still think the current behavior is very weird.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rustyhorde/vergen/issues/299/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rustyhorde/vergen/issues/299/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}